    "anomaly_root_cause_analysis": "Phase 25 reported Mode A production-only median of 7,010.84 ms and p95 of 28,538.89 ms. Audit confirms each measurement represented a SINGLE FRAME, but during the Phase 25 benchmark execution, a full 177-test unittest discover process was running concurrently in the background. Because Darknet YOLO on CPU uses full-core OpenCV dnn threads without GPU acceleration, background CPU saturation caused massive OS thread preemption, inflating single-frame latency up to 28+ seconds. Under clean, isolated conditions on Apple M1 CPU, true single-frame production latency is median 17856.1 ms and p95 30486.8 ms (YOLO detection takes ~13096.6 ms)."
